 "why": "fallback_stems is empty and two stems have no board: 185121 triggered the fallback (the engine SAM lane pass refuses this handheld 09-19 video) but kept its sam2-video track, because the yolo_chain_sam baseline track also has no final_board and fewer points (44 vs 55); 191900 has no throw, so it has an empty track, no cut, no baseline run and no final__ overlay. Choice: under the fixed rule, among the experiments with holdout verdict 'works' (cam-diff 73.0, lane-first 77.3, detector-tiling 78.6, sam2-video 90.5 holdout mean recall), sam2-video has the highest holdout mean recall (90.46 %, board_err <= 3 on 3/5, mean 2.5), so it is the one method for all 11 videos. appearance-prior (98.8 % holdout recall) is excluded by its 'partial' verdict (board <= 3 on only 2/5; 192636 got no board). No composition: no judge measured a lane stage on its own, and lane-first's holdout board misses (192142 3.4, 192636 5.2) are on the same two stems sam2-video misses (5.0, 5.5), so no holdout number justifies swapping the lane stage. Declared dependency: release_frame and pin_hit_frame come from work/cuts/cuts.json and set the SAM prompt window, the lane-pass segment and the reported window. For the dev stems those values were copied from the 09-19 labels, and for the holdout they are independent visual reads, so the dev numbers are not end-to-end and window_err is 0 by construction. track.py never opens a label file (static scan of all 57 imported local modules + an audit-hook run).",
